ssing artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged; and the driver's statement that he followed the navigation cites no evidence ID and, under POL-RD-08, carries no weight — although the outcome does not depend on it either way.\n\nThe GPS trace is clean for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 139 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, no gaps and no straight-line jumps over 500 m. Its 1.46 km excess is therefore a reliable measurement, no independent corroboration under POL-RD-07(ii) is required, and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. No other POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the identifiers all read TRP-03206, the timestamps are consistent, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a cited-but-absent artifact, and no charge line is unmatched. The 9.01% excess is far below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality line, so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not triggered and no conduct referral follows.\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03. That is party-relative — it leaves fare_breakdown.payment_status (CHARGED) and fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd (0.00) exactly as they are, so the fare stands as charged and nothing is refunded or restored. The monetary effect is nil, below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00. Confidence is 0.90, capped by the artifacts carrying the deciding facts — the GPS trace and the trip record, both at weight 1.0."
